    <!-- ========== The science ========== -->
    <section class="smf-sec smf-sec--mint" id="science" aria-labelledby="smf-science-title">
      <div class="smf-wrap">
        <p class="smf-eyebrow">The science</p>
        <h2 class="smf-h2" id="smf-science-title">Read the research yourself</h2>
        <div class="smf-copy smf-copy--narrow">
          <p>Everything here traces back to Dr. Marvin Cohen, a dentist who practiced for nearly 50 years and studied bad breath throughout his career. The research that followed is public, so you can read it for yourself.</p>
        </div>

        <ol class="smf-grid3 smf-steps">
          <li class="smf-card">
            <span class="smf-step__n" aria-hidden="true">1</span>
            <h3>Germs plus protein</h3>
            <p>Bacteria in the mouth break down protein and release sulfur gas. That gas is the smell.</p>
          </li>
          <li class="smf-card">
            <span class="smf-step__n" aria-hidden="true">2</span>
            <h3>Two solutions</h3>
            <p>Two solutions stay apart in the bottle until you pour, so the formula is fresh and active when it reaches your mouth.</p>
          </li>
          <li class="smf-card">
            <span class="smf-step__n" aria-hidden="true">3</span>
            <h3>Zinc blocks the gas</h3>
            <p>Zinc ions bind the sulfur compounds, for fresh breath for 24 hours with two rinses a day.</p>
          </li>
        </ol>

        <figure class="smf-banner">
          <picture>
